      "name": "primary_issue_category",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Categorizing the primary issue directly serves the query about improving satisfaction by grouping actionable problem types. However, groundedness is weakened: AMZ-0004 is labeled 'durability_issues' when the text describes a formulation change/quality complaint, not durability; and the dominant 'no_specific_issue' (170) risks conflating clearly issue-bearing reviews (e.g., availability/political-content complaints) with no-issue, though those are defensible readings for non-product-defect complaints."
    },
    {
      "name": "improvement_focus",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Partially useful as it separates satisfaction_drivers from dissatisfaction, but its issue-type values (design/quality/support/etc.) substantially overlap with primary_issue_category, making it a near-restatement for those rows. The satisfaction_drivers vs general_dissatisfaction split is a defensible reading grounded in the positive/negative tone of the source text."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_count",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A count of distinct issues gives a genuine severity/intensity axis to model on, useful for prioritizing. Values largely track the categorization (0 when no_specific_issue, 1 for a single complaint), so it is derivable from the text, though it inherits the miscategorization seen in AMZ-0004 and is somewhat redundant with the category columns."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.68,
  "source_groundedness": 0.63,
  "rationale": "The columns provide reasonable analytical axes (issue type, driver/dissatisfaction split, and issue intensity) that meaningfully support the query about improving satisfaction. Weaknesses: improvement_focus substantially overlaps with primary_issue_category for issue-typed rows, and there is at least one observed miscategorization (AMZ-0004 labeled durability when the complaint is a formulation/quality change). The heavy 'no_specific_issue'/'general_dissatisfaction' concentration is largely a defensible reading of non-defect complaints rather than a hallucination. Overall the set passes the two necessary conditions with moderate confidence."
}

